\begin{remark}[Physics notation: infrared behaviour]
The endpoint $T$ is the Wilsonian scale of the transfer, and the one-loop components are independent of it (Theorem \ref{thm:c8-L} (ii)). The insertions of $S^{(1)}$ along $Q$, $S$, $\Delta$, $P$, $M$, $\bar M$, $R$ converge at large distance, so these components may be computed at $T=\infty$ (Proposition \ref{prop:c8-Tsafe}); the special conformal $K_b$, whose Killing field $x^2b^m-2(b\cdot x)x^m$ grows quadratically, produces a large-distance logarithm, $\int_{|y|^2<T}|y|^{-4}d^4y$ growing as $\pi^2\log T$. Theorem \ref{thm:c8-K} states that the local operator $K_1(O)$ is nevertheless the same at every $T$, the $\log T$ residing in the Wilsonian flow of $O[T]$; in radial quantisation $K_b$ is the conjugate of $P_b$ (Corollary \ref{cor:c8-gram}).
\end{remark}

